		<text id="1" type="text/plain" rect="(192.0, 128.0, 150.0, 75.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">SERVICE HEALTH EXPLORATION</text>
		<text id="2" type="text/plain" rect="(477.0, -91.0, 150.0, 54.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">RETAIL EVENT &amp; SALES ANALYSIS</text>
		<text id="3" type="text/plain" rect="(271.0, 376.0, 150.0, 285.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">
DRIVE TIME COVERAGE ANALYSIS -
Finding: Raw coverage hours showed little direct relationship with Drive Time customer outcomes.

</text>
		<text id="4" type="text/plain" rect="(1070.0, 537.0, 150.0, 369.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">WORKLOAD ANALYSIS-
Finding: Adjusting coverage for transaction workload did not materially strengthen its relationship with Drive Time customer outcomes.




</text>
		<text id="5" type="text/plain" rect="(947.0, 362.0, 150.0, 117.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">OPERATIONAL-DRIVER RANKING
</text>
		<text id="6" type="text/plain" rect="(1493.0, 1.0, 150.0, 432.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">DRIVE TIME SERVICE HEALTH MODELING-
Finding: 
The reduced 8-feature Linear Regression matched the 15-feature model's cross-validation performance and was retained for greater simplicity




</text>
		<text id="7" type="text/plain" rect="(1472.75, 510.75, 150.0, 79.0)" font-family="Segoe UI" font-size="16">
DRIVE TIME NPS MODELING

